578
00:39:26,397 --> 00:39:32,654
great lessons, very important lessons, we ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to make us of those who, will benefit from them, and follow them.

579
00:39:33,350 --> 00:39:36,235
Our next stop is the Battle of the trench

580
00:39:37,350 --> 00:39:41,557
It also has the name of Ghazwat Ahzaab(غزوة الاحزاب),

581
00:39:42,413 --> 00:39:48,226
Ahzaab(احزاب) are the Confederates or the parties or the clans translated differently but

582
00:39:48,846 --> 00:39:51,877
these are the two names of the battle, Al-Khandaq(الخندق) and Al-Ahzaab(الاحزاب).

583
00:39:53,237 --> 00:39:54,361
What was the reason.?

584
00:39:54,877 --> 00:39:56,369
 Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق) says;

585
00:39:56,440 --> 00:40:00,601
اِنَّه’كَانَ الَّذِيْ حَزَّبَ الْاَحْزَابَ نَفَرً مِّنَّ الْيَهُوْدْ

586
00:40:01,190 --> 00:40:03,015
What happened at the Khandaq(خندق) was

587
00:40:03,076 --> 00:40:08,785
 that the group of Jews brought together a coalition of clans against the Messenger of Allah.

588
00:40:10,027 --> 00:40:14,567
So, this was a coalition that was pulled together by the Jews.

589
00:40:15,393 --> 00:40:19,004
They went to Makkah, they went to the tribes of Ghatafaan(غطفان),

590
00:40:19,127 --> 00:40:23,127
and they brought together, quite formidable army 10,000 strong,

591
00:40:23,784 --> 00:40:28,123
largest army ever assembled against Rasool Allah ﷺ up to that point.

592
00:40:29,511 --> 00:40:33,037
The agreement was that Ghatafaan(غطفان) would supply 6000 men

593
00:40:33,109 --> 00:40:38,593
 in exchange of the Jews paying them, the entire date harvest of Khaybar(خيبر) for one year.

594
00:40:38,956 --> 00:40:42,997
So, with Ghatafaan(غطفان), they're in it for money, they're mercenaries.

595
00:40:43,778 --> 00:40:49,430
The ones who had an intention of fighting against Muhammadﷺ were the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and the Yahood(يهود),

596
00:40:49,485 --> 00:40:55,692
 but Ghatafaan(غطفان), they were from far away and they just came in because the Jews promised them money.

597
00:40:56,144 --> 00:41:02,295
And the Jews would go to Makkah and the people of Makkah would ask them;

598
00:41:02,519 --> 00:41:03,681
because they are the learned men,

599
00:41:03,721 --> 00:41:07,741
see the Arabs used to consider that the Jews are the wise learned men,

600
00:41:07,846 --> 00:41:09,518
because they, the Arabs are illiterate.

601
00:41:10,354 --> 00:41:12,780
So, Abu Sufiyaan(ابو سفيان) and leaders of Quraish(قريش) said;

602
00:41:13,174 --> 00:41:16,526
Well, you are the learned man, you are the people of the book, so tell us,

603
00:41:17,503 --> 00:41:20,018
who is right us or Muhammad(محمد)?

604
00:41:20,645 --> 00:41:21,931
Who's on the right path?

605
00:41:22,750 --> 00:41:24,605
So, the Jews would tell them, you are.!

606
00:41:25,109 --> 00:41:26,406
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed.

607
00:41:26,937 --> 00:41:43,044
أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا نَصِيبًا مِنَ الْكِتَابِ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْجِبْتِ وَالطَّاغُوتِ وَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا هَٰؤُلَاءِ أَهْدَىٰ

608
00:41:43,846 --> 00:41:54,563
وَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا هَٰؤُلَاءِ أَهْدَىٰ مِنَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا سَبِيلًاَ ۝

609
00:41:55,196 --> 00:42:00,339
أُولَٰئِكَ الَّذِينَ لَعَنَهُمُ اللَّهُ ۖ

610
00:42:00,815 --> 00:42:07,764
وَمَنْ يَلْعَنِ اللَّهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُ نَصِيرًاَ۝

611
00:42:09,306 --> 00:42:11,918
Verse 51 and 52 Surat Tun Nissaa(سورة النساء) Allah says;

612
00:42:12,664 --> 00:42:16,106
Have you not seen those, who are given a portion of the Scripture,

613
00:42:16,687 --> 00:42:20,899
who believe, in superstition and false objects of worship,

614
00:42:21,679 --> 00:42:23,582
and say about the disbelievers.

615
00:42:23,960 --> 00:42:27,464
These are better guided then, the believers, as to the way.

616
00:42:28,351 --> 00:42:30,261
Those are the ones, whom Allah has cursed.

617
00:42:30,867 --> 00:42:34,862
And he, whom Allah curses, never will you find for him, a helper.

618
00:42:35,789 --> 00:42:41,330
Now one, would wonder what in the world, would make the Jews claim

619
00:42:41,679 --> 00:42:47,060
 that the pagan worshippers are more guided than the Muslims.

620
00:42:48,306 --> 00:42:53,598
I mean, the Jews have much more in common with the Muslims

621
00:42:53,645 --> 00:42:55,622
 than they have with the pagan worshippers.

622
00:42:55,662 --> 00:42:59,901
 I mean there's nothing in common between the people of the book and the pagan worshippers.

623
00:43:01,244 --> 00:43:03,591
But there is a lot in common between them and the Muslims.

624
00:43:04,595 --> 00:43:08,476
So, what would make them take such a position.

625
00:43:09,064 --> 00:43:11,889
And that would go back to the reasons that we talked about earlier,

626
00:43:12,024 --> 00:43:16,894
the stand that the Jews took from very early on, against Rasool Allah ﷺ

627
00:43:16,961 --> 00:43:19,918
for the various reasons, of jealousy and hatred.

628
00:43:20,453 --> 00:43:25,362
 Rasool Allah ﷺ was following the news and again, we said that he had his men spread out all over,

629
00:43:26,064 --> 00:43:27,510
gathering intelligence for him.

630
00:43:28,017 --> 00:43:32,092
So, the news reached to Rasool Allah ﷺ prior to them, advancing towards Madina

631
00:43:32,132 --> 00:43:35,331
that huge army is coming your way.

632
00:43:36,110 --> 00:43:39,314
Rasool Allah ﷺ hold a Shura(شورى), session.

633
00:43:40,876 --> 00:43:45,286
And Salman Farsi رضي الله عنه, has a suggestion, he said;

634
00:43:45,892 --> 00:43:55,472
يَا رَسُوْل الله، اِنَّ اِذَ كُنَّا بِاَرْضِ الْفَارِسْ وَتَخَوَّفْنَا الْخَيْلْ، خَنْدَقْنَا عَلَيْنَا فَهَل لَّكَ يَا رَسُوْل الله اَنْ تُخَنْدِقْ

635
00:43:56,220 --> 00:44:00,433
He said: O Messenger of Allah in our land in Persia.

636
00:44:00,814 --> 00:44:03,450
 If we fear, the cavalry.

637
00:44:04,053 --> 00:44:07,529
 We would dig a trench, or a moat.

638
00:44:08,329 --> 00:44:13,105
O messenger of Allah, why don't we dig a moat, a trench.

639
00:44:13,720 --> 00:44:16,041
Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Muslims, liked the idea,

640
00:44:16,595 --> 00:44:18,728
and the project started.

641
00:44:19,462 --> 00:44:24,908
Now, it would have been impossible for them to dig this moat, all around Madina,

642
00:44:25,328 --> 00:44:27,495
because they just didn't have the manpower for that,

643
00:44:27,551 --> 00:44:30,860
so they had to choose the locations which were vulnerable.

644
00:44:31,564 --> 00:44:34,535
Now that location was north of Madina,

645
00:44:34,970 --> 00:44:38,456
which would sound strange because Makkah is to the south,

646
00:44:38,985 --> 00:44:44,081
but the thing is that Madina, had a natural protection from the east and west,

647
00:44:44,579 --> 00:44:47,922
and that was what is called, Al-Harrah(الحرة), these are volcanic tracks,

648
00:44:48,376 --> 00:44:49,787
tracks of volcanic rock,

649
00:44:50,423 --> 00:44:56,743
very sharp, very edgy and boulders all over, so it's difficult for an army to march through.

650
00:44:57,829 --> 00:45:01,894
And then from the south, you have the dwellings, the farmland,

651
00:45:02,095 --> 00:45:04,936
which also makes it difficult to penetrate.

652
00:45:05,539 --> 00:45:07,547
So, the danger is from the north.

653
00:45:08,362 --> 00:45:11,006
And that's where, they dug the trench.

654
00:45:11,798 --> 00:45:17,162
Every 10 men were given 40 feet of land to dig.

655
00:45:17,898 --> 00:45:20,501
And they split into groups and they start the work.

656
00:45:21,579 --> 00:45:22,674
It was very difficult,

657
00:45:23,285 --> 00:45:27,217
The Muslims were hungry, they were poor, there was lack of food.

658
00:45:27,859 --> 00:45:31,870
And there was lack of numbers too, to dig this trench.

659
00:45:32,573 --> 00:45:36,765
Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه, he said the Messenger of Allah went out to the trench

660
00:45:37,510 --> 00:45:40,826
and found that the Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) and the Ansaar(انصار) were busy digging.

661
00:45:41,354 --> 00:45:45,830
It was a very cold morning, and they had no slaves to do that work for them.

662
00:45:46,541 --> 00:45:50,873
When he saw, what they were suffering from, the hard labor and their hunger, he said;

663
00:45:51,369 --> 00:45:55,076
O Allah, their life is indeed that of the afterlife,

664
00:45:55,473 --> 00:45:57,404
forgive the Ansaar(انصار) and the Muhajiroon(مهاجرون).

665
00:45:58,369 --> 00:46:00,181
They're having difficulty in Duniyah(دنيا), but

666
00:46:00,698 --> 00:46:04,634
their life doesn't belong to this world, it belongs to the afterlife.

667
00:46:05,463 --> 00:46:09,278
Rasool Allah ﷺ himself participated in the digging.

668
00:46:09,762 --> 00:46:11,904
 Al-Bara'a(البرآء) narrates in Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ),

669
00:46:12,322 --> 00:46:15,630
لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمَ الْاَحْزَابِ وَخَنْدَقَ رَسُوْلُ الله صَلى الله عليه وسلم

670
00:46:15,876 --> 00:46:21,138
رَاَيْتُه، يَنْقُلْ مِنْ تَرَابِ الْخَنْدَقْ حَتَّى وَارِى عَنِّيْ اَلْغُبَارْ جِلْدَةَ بَطْنِه

671
00:46:21,757 --> 00:46:25,016
On the day of Al-Ahzaad(احزاب), when Rasool Allah ﷺ was digging the trench,

672
00:46:25,056 --> 00:46:31,911
I saw him, carrying dirt, until there was so much dirt on his stomach, I couldn't see his skin anymore.

673
00:46:33,038 --> 00:46:38,350
Rasool Allah ﷺ was right there with his followers in the field, working with them.

674
00:46:38,549 --> 00:46:41,380
This is the leadership example that Rasool Allah ﷺ is giving us.

675
00:46:41,944 --> 00:46:46,313
He wasn't aloof from the people, he wouldn't treat himself specially,

676
00:46:46,663 --> 00:46:49,263
he was trying to be one of them.

677
00:46:49,741 --> 00:46:53,392
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was the best of humanity صلى الله عليه وسلم.

678
00:46:54,054 --> 00:46:58,607
Rasool Allah ﷺ would get so hungry, he would have to tie a stone to his stomach.

679
00:46:59,522 --> 00:47:05,380
You know to suppress the hunger to elevate the pain, he would tie this rock to his stomach

680
00:47:05,496 --> 00:47:10,445
 that was how difficult it was on him and how hungry, he صلى الله عليه وسلم was.

681
00:47:11,588 --> 00:47:17,499
But his spirit was high, and he would elevate the spirits of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, and he would chant with them,

682
00:47:17,916 --> 00:47:20,151
so they would recite these lines of poetry,

683
00:47:20,572 --> 00:47:24,482
and Rasool Allah ﷺ would go along with them and recite these words they would say,

684
00:47:24,807 --> 00:47:28,935
"O Allah, without you we would not have been well guided.....

685
00:47:29,510 --> 00:47:31,736
nor would we have been charitable.....

686
00:47:31,919 --> 00:47:33,629
Nor would we have prayed.....

687
00:47:33,979 --> 00:47:36,431
so do send tranquility upon us.....

688
00:47:36,732 --> 00:47:39,375
And make us stand firm, when we meet the foe.....

689
00:47:39,557 --> 00:47:40,751
They have wronged us.....

690
00:47:40,971 --> 00:47:43,162
 If they want trouble, we will meet them.....

691
00:47:43,510 --> 00:47:45,797
And Rasool Allah ﷺ would stretch the final words.

692
00:47:46,807 --> 00:47:48,322
They're guards around the clock,

693
00:47:48,807 --> 00:47:50,982
guarding the trench and guarding Madina,

694
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:55,827
and the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would take turns in guarding

695
00:47:56,432 --> 00:48:00,489
the difficulties were increasing, rather than decreasing.

696
00:48:01,063 --> 00:48:06,394
You have this army coming forward, made up of Quraish(قريش) and Ghatafaan(غطفان).

697
00:48:06,985 --> 00:48:14,270
And then there was a very serious problem, and this couldn't have come in a worse time.

698
00:48:15,258 --> 00:48:18,246
The dwellings of Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

699
00:48:18,828 --> 00:48:26,424
The last Jewish tribe remaining in Madina, were part of the protection,

700
00:48:26,989 --> 00:48:30,551
 were part of the plan of protection that Rasool Allah ﷺ had for Madina.

701
00:48:31,242 --> 00:48:39,375
So, their fortresses were used as a protection from the army advancing from that area.

702
00:48:40,454 --> 00:48:42,828
Rasool Allah ﷺ was receiving news

703
00:48:43,535 --> 00:48:48,781
that Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه), themselves were betraying their agreement with Rasool Allah ﷺ

704
00:48:48,847 --> 00:48:51,871
 and were going to join with the Confederates.

705
00:48:52,689 --> 00:48:57,546
This would have been a disaster because they were supposed to be part of the protection,

706
00:48:57,633 --> 00:49:01,822
So if that gate is opened, then the Muslims are going to be in serious trouble.

707
00:49:03,557 --> 00:49:07,996
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ send Al-Zubair Bin Awwam(الزبير بن عوام) to investigate the matter.

708
00:49:08,626 --> 00:49:11,265
Al-Zubair Bin Awwam(الزبير بن عوام) brings back information that

709
00:49:11,822 --> 00:49:18,320
they are bringing in their livestock, and they are paving their roads,

710
00:49:18,704 --> 00:49:21,598
which is an indication of preparation for war.

711
00:49:23,095 --> 00:49:26,084
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to investigate the matter further,

712
00:49:26,124 --> 00:49:32,188
so he sends Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد بن معاذ), Sa'ad Ibn Ubadah(سعد بن عباده), Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) and Khawaat Bin Jubair(خوات بن جبير).

713
00:49:32,657 --> 00:49:35,994
He told them, go and investigate the matter

714
00:49:36,034 --> 00:49:43,103
 and bring me news of whether Quraidha( قريظه) have betrayed, or broken their agreement with me.

715
00:49:43,501 --> 00:49:49,468
If that's the case, do not weaken the people come and deliver the news to me, secretly.

716
00:49:50,251 --> 00:49:54,817
If you find that they are still up to their word and agreement,

717
00:49:55,404 --> 00:49:59,504
and they're keeping the agreement, then, make the news public.

718
00:50:00,282 --> 00:50:04,677
And we can see here, the lesson, we learned a lesson here from Rasool Allah ﷺ that

719
00:50:05,307 --> 00:50:09,264
sometimes you want to keep away some news from the people.

720
00:50:10,001 --> 00:50:15,002
If it's detrimental news, if it's a news that would demoralize them,

721
00:50:15,329 --> 00:50:20,041
if it would weaken them, it might be Muslaha(مصلحة) to keep it away from the army.

722
00:50:20,985 --> 00:50:24,144
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to keep it secret, if that was the case.

723
00:50:24,954 --> 00:50:30,059
But if it's good news that they are still keeping the agreement, then make it public.

724
00:50:31,063 --> 00:50:35,460
Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد بن معاذ), Sa'ad Ibn Ubadah(سعد بن عباده), Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) and Khawaat(خوات بن جبير), they go there, they come back

725
00:50:35,969 --> 00:50:38,721
and they tell Rasool Allah ﷺ two words.

726
00:50:38,809 --> 00:50:39,979
Azal Wal Qarrah(عضل والقارة).

727
00:50:40,720 --> 00:50:42,752
Azal Wal Qarrah(عضل والقارة), if you remember,

728
00:50:43,251 --> 00:50:47,400
are the two tribes that betrayed the men, whom were sent by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

729
00:50:47,503 --> 00:50:49,273
the ones who betrayed the men and killed them.

730
00:50:50,094 --> 00:50:55,614
So, this was an indication from these men that Quraidha( قريظه) have broken the agreement

731
00:50:55,789 --> 00:51:01,598
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ got the point, and made preparations for that.

732
00:51:02,189 --> 00:51:05,343
Rasool Allah ﷺ sends out two groups,

733
00:51:06,001 --> 00:51:11,174
one 200 men, the other one 300 men as guards,

734
00:51:11,954 --> 00:51:17,005
and they would go around the area of Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه) to show them that we are still here,

735
00:51:17,045 --> 00:51:19,172
and we're still strong, and we're willing to fight.

736
00:51:19,702 --> 00:51:21,042
So, it was a show of strength,

737
00:51:21,907 --> 00:51:30,856
and the Muslims were able to intercept 20 Camel loads of Dates Figs and barley,

738
00:51:31,372 --> 00:51:36,735
that we're going towards the army of the Ahzaab(احزاب)

739
00:51:37,551 --> 00:51:41,167
and their point of origin was Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

740
00:51:41,739 --> 00:51:47,047
So, it makes it clear that Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه) have betrayed Rasool Allah ﷺ, they have committed treason.

741
00:51:47,614 --> 00:51:51,303
They are now supplying the army of the enemy.

742
00:51:52,645 --> 00:51:56,363
So, it was very difficult on the Muslims, extremely difficult,

743
00:51:56,456 --> 00:51:59,524
 probably the most difficult situation, they've been through.

744
00:52:00,130 --> 00:52:02,760
Allahعَزّوجَلّ describes it, to us. Allah says;

745
00:52:03,442 --> 00:52:11,825
إِذْ جَاءُوكُمْ مِنْ فَوْقِكُمْ وَمِنْ أَسْفَلَ مِنْكُمْ

746
00:52:12,158 --> 00:52:22,316
وَإِذْ زَاغَتِ الْأَبْصَارُ وَبَلَغَتِ الْقُلُوبُ الْحَنَاجِرَ وَتَظُنُّونَ بِاللَّهِ الظُّنُونَا۝

747
00:52:23,127 --> 00:52:27,976
Remember, when they came at you from above you, and from below you.

748
00:52:28,373 --> 00:52:32,228
And when eyes shifted in fear and hearts reach to the throats,

749
00:52:32,611 --> 00:52:36,080
and you assumed about Allah various assumptions.

750
00:52:37,533 --> 00:52:41,974
So here, the eyes were shifting in fear, you know there was this disorientation going on.

751
00:52:42,721 --> 00:52:45,994
And Allah says that the hearts reached the throats

752
00:52:46,685 --> 00:52:49,280
which means that the hearts were pounding so fast.

753
00:52:49,564 --> 00:52:52,018
It was as if you can feel it in your throat.

754
00:52:52,097 --> 00:52:54,899
That was how difficult the situation was.

755
00:52:55,674 --> 00:52:59,052
And you assumed about Allah various assumptions.

756
00:52:59,721 --> 00:53:03,018
So, some people were making assumptions about the Allah,

757
00:53:03,058 --> 00:53:09,628
like Allah has promised us, in vain and that Allahعَزّوجَلّ will not give us victory

758
00:53:09,668 --> 00:53:13,279
 and that this religion is not true and we made a mistake,

759
00:53:13,964 --> 00:53:16,327
so all of these doubts were coming into the hearts

760
00:53:17,424 --> 00:53:22,369
and obviously the ones who are having these dangerous doubts in the religion were Munafiqoon(منافقون).

761
00:53:22,939 --> 00:53:25,693
Allahعَزّوجَلّ also says and these Ayaat(آيات) are from Surat Ul Ahzaab(سورة الاحزاب).

762
00:53:26,299 --> 00:53:35,560
وَلَمَّا رَأَى الْمُؤْمِنُونَ الْأَحْزَابَ قَالُوا هَٰذَا مَا وَعَدَنَا اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ

763
00:53:35,761 --> 00:53:38,666
 وَصَدَقَ اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ ۚ

764
00:53:38,825 --> 00:53:45,709
وَمَا زَادَهُمْ إِلَّا إِيمَانًا وَتَسْلِيمًاَ۝

765
00:53:46,195 --> 00:53:49,017
And when the believers saw the companies, they said;

766
00:53:49,476 --> 00:53:52,433
This is what Allah and His Messenger had promised us.

767
00:53:52,991 --> 00:53:55,196
And Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth.

768
00:53:55,788 --> 00:53:58,464
And it increased them only in faith and acceptance.

769
00:53:59,555 --> 00:54:01,065
This was the response of the believers.

770
00:54:02,554 --> 00:54:05,839
When the believers saw all of these dangers being thrown at them,

771
00:54:07,038 --> 00:54:08,624
that increased their Eeman(ايمان),

772
00:54:09,398 --> 00:54:13,285
rather than decreased it because they knew that Allahعَزّوجَلّ will test them,

773
00:54:13,333 --> 00:54:14,912
so they saw this as part of the test.

774
00:54:14,952 --> 00:54:18,016
 Therefore, it only confirms what we already knew would happen.

775
00:54:18,476 --> 00:54:24,340
But with the Munafiqeen(منافقين), it made them doubt even more, in the authenticity of Islam.

776
00:54:24,741 --> 00:54:29,346
So, you can see how one event brought forth different reactions from the two camps,

777
00:54:29,460 --> 00:54:31,528
the believers and the non-believers.

778
00:54:31,991 --> 00:54:34,711
See when it comes to fear, the fear was across the board,

779
00:54:34,751 --> 00:54:37,549
 the believers were afraid and the Munafiqeen(منافقين) were afraid,

780
00:54:37,671 --> 00:54:40,136
but what is different is the reaction to that fear.

781
00:54:40,545 --> 00:54:42,811
See fear is a natural human instinct,

782
00:54:43,466 --> 00:54:45,596
it is natural for human being to feel fear.

783
00:54:46,154 --> 00:54:49,141
Musa عليه السّلام himself felt fear,

784
00:54:49,482 --> 00:54:52,141
فَأَوْجَسَ فِي نَفْسِهِ خِيفَةً مُوسَىٰ

785
00:54:52,181 --> 00:54:55,210
Allahعَزّوجَلّ said that he felt fear in his heart.

786
00:54:55,577 --> 00:54:59,877
But the thing is, with Musa عليه السّلام the fear was restricted to the heart.

787
00:54:59,928 --> 00:55:03,807
It didn't show up on his actions, his actions were full of Eeman(ايمان).

788
00:55:04,966 --> 00:55:08,642
So, that's the difference between Al-Mu'menoon(المؤمنون) and Al-Munafiqoon(منافقون).

789
00:55:09,163 --> 00:55:12,807
The Munafiqoon(منافقون) acted negatively upon their fear,

790
00:55:13,123 --> 00:55:15,190
while the believers acted positively,

791
00:55:15,357 --> 00:55:19,353
they said this is what Allahعَزّوجَلّ has promised us, we expected this would happen.

792
00:55:19,670 --> 00:55:20,875
Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق) said;

793
00:55:21,248 --> 00:55:27,845
There upon, the anxiety and fear increased their enemy came at them from above and below,

794
00:55:28,326 --> 00:55:30,386
so the Muslims were very confused

795
00:55:30,823 --> 00:55:35,954
 dissension arose, to the point where Muattib Bin Qushair(معتب بن قشير) commented,

796
00:55:36,420 --> 00:55:41,531
Muhammad(محمد) used to promise us that we would eat the treasures of Kisra(كسرى) and Caesar.

797
00:55:41,807 --> 00:55:44,467
And now we don't even feel safe going to the toilet.

798
00:55:44,966 --> 00:55:47,721
So, this is an example of the response of a Munafiq(منافق).

799
00:55:48,263 --> 00:55:50,165
He said, what is Muhammadﷺ talking about?

800
00:55:50,404 --> 00:55:53,783
Rasool Allah ﷺ and we will talk about this, when they were digging the trench.

801
00:55:54,435 --> 00:56:00,604
He gave glad tidings that this Ummah(امة) would open the Persian Empire and the Roman Empire.

802
00:56:01,136 --> 00:56:02,787
He said, What is Muhammad(محمد) talking about.?

803
00:56:02,818 --> 00:56:05,787
We can't even feel safe going to the toilet and he's promising us,

804
00:56:06,136 --> 00:56:11,454
 that we will conquer lands, thousands of kilometers away from us,

805
00:56:12,529 --> 00:56:17,773
and the Ayah(آية) of Qur'an described, Al-Munafiqoon(المنافقون) and I'll go through this Ayaat(آيات)

806
00:56:17,830 --> 00:56:22,695
because these are the characteristics of Munafiqoon(منافقون) yesterday, and today, they don't change.

807
00:56:23,013 --> 00:56:28,195
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, these are Ayaat(آيات) thirteen(13) through 20 in Surat Ul Ahzaab(سورة الاحزاب)

808
00:56:28,748 --> 00:56:39,594
وَإِذْ قَالَتْ طَائِفَةٌ مِنْهُمْ يَا أَهْلَ يَثْرِبَ لَا مُقَامَ لَكُمْ فَارْجِعُوا ۚ

809
00:56:39,927 --> 00:56:46,303
وَيَسْتَأْذِنُ فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمُ النَّبِيَّ يَقُولُونَ

810
00:56:46,589 --> 00:56:53,197
 يَقُولُونَ إِنَّ بُيُوتَنَا عَوْرَةٌ وَمَا هِيَ بِعَوْرَةٍ ۖ

811
00:56:53,515 --> 00:56:59,013
إِنْ يُرِيدُونَ إِلَّا فِرَارًا۝

812
00:56:59,576 --> 00:57:01,219
And when a faction of them said;

813
00:57:01,716 --> 00:57:02,959
Oh, people of Yasrib(يثرب).

814
00:57:03,435 --> 00:57:06,548
There's no stability for you here, so return home.

815
00:57:07,388 --> 00:57:10,619
And a party of them asked permission of the Prophet saying,

816
00:57:11,038 --> 00:57:13,424
indeed, our houses are exposed,

817
00:57:14,054 --> 00:57:17,539
while they were not exposed they did not intend, except to flee.

818
00:57:18,085 --> 00:57:20,945
So, the Munafiqoon(منافقون) here don't want to stay next to the trench.

819
00:57:21,132 --> 00:57:24,573
They don't want to stay in the camp, they want to go back home and the excuse is,

820
00:57:24,929 --> 00:57:26,479
we need to go and defend the homes.

821
00:57:27,929 --> 00:57:30,061
So, they pretending that they're going to go and fight,

822
00:57:30,445 --> 00:57:33,990
but Allahعَزّوجَلّ said, they did not intend except to flee.

823
00:57:34,366 --> 00:57:36,177
That was their intention to run away.

824
00:57:36,804 --> 00:57:46,025
وَلَوْ دُخِلَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنْ أَقْطَارِهَا ثُمَّ سُئِلُوا الْفِتْنَةَ لَآتَوْهَا

825
00:57:46,287 --> 00:57:53,538
لَآتَوْهَا وَمَا تَلَبَّثُوا بِهَا إِلَّا يَسِيرًا۝

826
00:57:54,380 --> 00:57:58,701
And if they had been entered upon from all its surrounding regions

827
00:57:58,791 --> 00:58:01,966
 and Fitnah(فتنة) had been demanded of them,

828
00:58:02,177 --> 00:58:06,162
they would have done it and not hesitated over it, except briefly.

829
00:58:06,818 --> 00:58:10,918
This Ayah(آية) means that the Munafiqoon(منافقون), if they are pressured a bit,

830
00:58:11,299 --> 00:58:12,402
they're going to give up Islam,

831
00:58:12,443 --> 00:58:15,359
if the enemy asked them to become non Muslim, they're going to do that.

832
00:58:15,896 --> 00:58:24,448
وَلَقَدْ كَانُوا عَاهَدُوا اللَّهَ مِنْ قَبْلُ لَا يُوَلُّونَ الْأَدْبَارَ ۚ

833
00:58:24,689 --> 00:58:28,665
وَكَانَ عَهْدُ اللَّهِ مَسْئُولًاَ۝

834
00:58:29,173 --> 00:58:37,366
قُلْ لَنْ يَنْفَعَكُمُ الْفِرَارُ إِنْ فَرَرْتُمْ مِنَ الْمَوْتِ أَوِ الْقَتْلِ

835
00:58:37,692 --> 00:58:42,615
 وَإِذًا لَا تُمَتَّعُونَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًاَ۝

836
00:58:43,313 --> 00:58:48,077
And they had already promised Allah before, not to turn their backs.

837
00:58:48,733 --> 00:58:51,315
And ever is the promise to Allah questioned.

838
00:58:52,358 --> 00:58:58,282
Say Never will fleeing benefit you, if you should flee from death or killing.

839
00:58:58,702 --> 00:59:03,387
And then if you did, you would not be given enjoyment of life, except for a little.

840
00:59:03,749 --> 00:59:05,768
This Aayah(آية), Allah is saying.

841
00:59:06,307 --> 00:59:09,362
 The meaning of the Aayah(آية), death is destined upon you.

842
00:59:09,905 --> 00:59:12,916
So, running away from it, wouldn't change it, a bit.

843
00:59:13,217 --> 00:59:15,634
Now let's assume that it's even going to change it.

844
00:59:15,685 --> 00:59:16,960
How long are you going to live?

845
00:59:17,155 --> 00:59:19,489
your life as a human being is very short.

846
00:59:19,874 --> 00:59:21,468
So, what are you running away from.?

847
00:59:21,841 --> 00:59:22,881
Then Allah says;

848
00:59:23,436 --> 00:59:34,579
قُلْ مَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَعْصِمُكُمْ مِنَ اللَّهِ إِنْ أَرَادَ بِكُمْ سُوءًا أَوْ أَرَادَ بِكُمْ رَحْمَةً ۚ

849
00:59:34,967 --> 00:59:43,595
وَلَا يَجِدُونَ لَهُمْ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ وَلِيًّا وَلَا نَصِيرًا۝

850
00:59:43,991 --> 00:59:47,849
Say, who is it that can protect you, from Allah.

851
00:59:48,178 --> 00:59:51,753
If He intends for you an ill or intends for you, a mercy,

852
00:59:52,350 --> 00:59:57,842
and they will not find for themselves besides Allah, any protector, or any helper.

853
00:59:58,709 --> 01:00:01,188
The Munafiqoon(منافقون) are looking for help, the wrong place.

854
01:00:01,678 --> 01:00:05,120
They're looking for help from the Yahood(يهود), they're looking for help from Al-Kuffar(كفار).

855
01:00:05,167 --> 01:00:08,263
Allah is saying, only Allah is An-Nafiah(النافع) and Adh-Dhaar(الضار)

856
01:00:08,306 --> 01:00:11,175
only Allah can benefit you and only Allah can harm you.

857
01:00:12,319 --> 01:00:13,683
And then Allah says;

858
01:00:13,912 --> 01:00:24,825
قَدْ يَعْلَمُ اللَّهُ الْمُعَوِّقِينَ مِنْكُمْ وَالْقَائِلِينَ لِإِخْوَانِهِمْ هَلُمَّ إِلَيْنَا ۖ

859
01:00:25,182 --> 01:00:29,867
وَلَا يَأْتُونَ الْبَأْسَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًاَ

860
01:00:30,024 --> 01:00:32,492
أَشِحَّةً عَلَيْكُمْ ۖ

861
01:00:32,807 --> 01:00:45,849
فَإِذَا جَاءَ الْخَوْفُ رَأَيْتَهُمْ يَنْظُرُونَ إِلَيْكَ تَدُورُ أَعْيُنُهُمْ كَالَّذِي يُغْشَىٰ عَلَيْهِ مِنَ الْمَوْتِ ۖ

862
01:00:46,294 --> 01:00:55,243
فَإِذَا ذَهَبَ الْخَوْفُ سَلَقُوكُمْ بِأَلْسِنَةٍ حِدَادٍ أَشِحَّةً عَلَى الْخَيْرِ ۚ

863
01:00:55,934 --> 01:01:07,199
أُولَٰئِكَ لَمْ يُؤْمِنُوا فَأَحْبَطَ اللَّهُ أَعْمَالَهُمْ ۚ وَكَانَ ذَٰلِكَ عَلَى اللَّهِ يَسِيرًاَ۝

864
01:01:07,641 --> 01:01:10,847
Already, Allah knows the hinders among you,

865
01:01:11,203 --> 01:01:14,248
and those hypocrites, who say to their brothers.

866
01:01:14,641 --> 01:01:20,202
Come to us, and do not go to battle except for a few, in disposed towards you.

867
01:01:20,609 --> 01:01:21,942
And when fear comes,

868
01:01:22,132 --> 01:01:26,196
see this is the reaction when it's in times of difficulty, what do they do.?

869
01:01:26,402 --> 01:01:29,885
And when fear comes, you see they looking at you.

870
01:01:30,297 --> 01:01:33,894
Their eyes revolving like one being overcome by death,

871
01:01:34,343 --> 01:01:40,765
but when fear departs, they lash you with sharp tongues, in disposed towards any good.

872
01:01:41,625 --> 01:01:44,338
This is a quality of Nifaq(نفاق),

873
01:01:44,846 --> 01:01:50,475
 in times of fear, their eyes are rotating, they're going around in circles because of fear,

874
01:01:50,647 --> 01:01:52,508
they're confused, they're afraid.

875
01:01:52,754 --> 01:01:56,270
But when fear goes away, they're very loud, they talk a lot.

876
01:01:57,151 --> 01:01:58,214
And then Allah says;

877
01:01:58,508 --> 01:02:05,032
Those have not believed, so Allah has rendered their deeds worthless and ever is that for Allah, easy.

878
01:02:05,803 --> 01:02:09,758
Therefore, don't go by what people say in times of peace.

879
01:02:09,845 --> 01:02:12,935
See, in times of peace, anybody and everybody can talk.

880
01:02:14,016 --> 01:02:17,316
But what happens in times of difficulty, in times of Fitna(فتنه).

881
01:02:17,984 --> 01:02:21,774
The Munafiqoon(منافقون) stay quiet, they're afraid they're terrified.

882
01:02:22,562 --> 01:02:25,471
But when fear goes away they lash out, at everyone.

883
01:02:25,937 --> 01:02:29,502
They start criticizing so and so, talking against so and so.

884
01:02:30,078 --> 01:02:32,455
So, the bravado only comes out in the wrong time.

885
01:02:33,656 --> 01:02:37,707
يَحْسَبُونَ الْأَحْزَابَ لَمْ يَذْهَبُوا ۖ

886
01:02:37,945 --> 01:02:49,925
وَإِنْ يَأْتِ الْأَحْزَابُ يَوَدُّوا لَوْ أَنَّهُمْ بَادُونَ فِي الْأَعْرَابِ يَسْأَلُونَ عَنْ أَنْبَائِكُمْ ۖ

887
01:02:50,648 --> 01:02:53,774
They think, the companies have not yet withdrawn.

888
01:02:54,023 --> 01:02:55,978
And if the companies should come again.

889
01:02:56,398 --> 01:03:02,032
They would wish they were in the desert among the Bedouins inquiring from a far about your news.

890
01:03:02,273 --> 01:03:06,604
These Munafiqoon(منافقون), if the armies would attack Madina once again,

891
01:03:06,668 --> 01:03:10,269
they would wish that they were not in Madina and they were with the Bedouins

892
01:03:10,663 --> 01:03:15,625
watching the news on their TV sets, listening to it on their radio sets.

893
01:03:16,507 --> 01:03:20,348
They would wish they could hold the remote control in their hands and flip through the channels

894
01:03:20,679 --> 01:03:23,776
and listen to the news or watch the news about the Muslims,

895
01:03:24,054 --> 01:03:25,499
but they don't want to be there.

896
01:03:26,491 --> 01:03:27,400
Then Allah says;

897
01:03:27,835 --> 01:03:35,438
وَلَوْ كَانُوا فِيكُمْ مَا قَاتَلُوا إِلَّا قَلِيلاً۝

898
01:03:35,960 --> 01:03:37,562
And if they should be among you,

899
01:03:37,898 --> 01:03:40,275
they would not fight except for a little.

900
01:03:41,194 --> 01:03:42,692
These are signs of Nifaq(نفاق).

901
01:03:43,257 --> 01:03:44,735
The Muslims were suffering hunger.

902
01:03:45,444 --> 01:03:48,080
In Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ), Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) said;

903
01:03:48,585 --> 01:03:50,937
"They would bring a handful of barley,

904
01:03:51,351 --> 01:03:55,377
and some ill smelling fat, as a meal for them,

905
01:03:55,718 --> 01:03:59,877
hungry as they were, it struck in their throats, and smell bad.

906
01:04:00,398 --> 01:04:01,319
So, what was the food.?

907
01:04:01,620 --> 01:04:04,747
Some barley, and then they had animal fat,

908
01:04:05,429 --> 01:04:11,902
which was very old long expired, smell bad, it was rotten.

909
01:04:12,226 --> 01:04:15,092
And they would swallow it and it would stick to the throat,

910
01:04:15,132 --> 01:04:18,370
 you know how animal fat sticks to the throat, if you eat fat,

911
01:04:18,944 --> 01:04:20,051
especially if it's cold.

912
01:04:20,504 --> 01:04:23,916
You know it sticks to your mouth and your teeth in the throat, and all.

913
01:04:24,163 --> 01:04:26,729
And because it smelled bad they could still smell it.

914
01:04:27,898 --> 01:04:31,053
But they were so hungry that they were eating this horrible food.

915
01:04:32,413 --> 01:04:35,931
Al-Waqadie(الواقعدي) describes the situation that was going on

916
01:04:35,978 --> 01:04:39,845
and he talks about the fear that everybody was feeling

917
01:04:39,894 --> 01:04:42,025
the hunger that everyone was feeling,

918
01:04:42,169 --> 01:04:47,715
the low spirits, especially because of what the Munafiqoon(منافقون) were doing

919
01:04:48,163 --> 01:04:50,604
bombarding the Muslims with only bad news.

920
01:04:51,199 --> 01:04:55,481
And then you have this disaster coming from the quarters of Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه)

921
01:04:55,577 --> 01:04:59,725
the news that they have broken their agreement with Rasool Allah ﷺ, so it was very difficult.

922
01:05:00,773 --> 01:05:04,349
And the Muslims had to work day and night, I mean, Muhammad Ibn Maslama(محمد ابن مسلمه) said;

923
01:05:04,444 --> 01:05:06,635
كَانَ لَيْلُنَا بِالْخَنْدَقِ نَهَارًا

924
01:05:06,929 --> 01:05:10,349
Our night during the Khandaq(خندق) was daytime,

925
01:05:10,601 --> 01:05:14,586
meaning we had to work around the clock night was no different than day.

926
01:05:15,710 --> 01:05:19,768
So, it was very stressful and you know when people are lacking sleep

927
01:05:19,944 --> 01:05:23,359
how they lose concentration and they fail to think straight.

928
01:05:23,923 --> 01:05:27,391
So, Allah was testing them, Allah was testing them, to the limit.

929
01:05:27,788 --> 01:05:34,345
Fighting did occur, you had duels you had enemy, trying to break through the trench from time to time,

930
01:05:34,819 --> 01:05:40,692
one incident that happened, a challenge to single combat was Amr Bin Abdu Woodh(عمرو بن عبد ود),

931
01:05:40,883 --> 01:05:45,034
 now Amr Bin Abdu Woodh(عمرو بن عبد ود) was one of the heroes of Quraish(قريش), strong powerful man.

932
01:05:46,038 --> 01:05:47,386
So, he challenges the Muslims,

933
01:05:48,241 --> 01:05:49,845
send me forth, one of your men.

934
01:05:50,452 --> 01:05:52,487
The one who went for it was Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب).

935
01:05:53,679 --> 01:05:55,135
Amr(عمرو) ask him, Who are you.?

936
01:05:55,468 --> 01:05:56,719
He said: I am Ali(علي).

937
01:05:57,069 --> 01:05:58,641
He said Ali(علي), the son of Abdul Mannaf(عبدالمناف).

938
01:05:58,726 --> 01:06:00,821
He said, No, I'm Ali(علي), the son of Abu Talib(ابو طالب).

939
01:06:01,804 --> 01:06:02,707
He said, nephew.

940
01:06:03,234 --> 01:06:08,845
There are among your uncle's, men who are more senior than you, more mature than you.

941
01:06:09,345 --> 01:06:11,845
 I feel sorry spilling your blood.

942
01:06:13,023 --> 01:06:16,019
Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) said: But I don't feel sorry spilling your blood.

943
01:06:16,882 --> 01:06:24,478
Amr Bin Abdu Woodh(عمرو بن عبد ود) wanted somebody more senior to come and meet him stronger, with more experience.

944
01:06:25,023 --> 01:06:29,432
And he said: I wouldn't want to spill your blood, my young nephew.

945
01:06:30,491 --> 01:06:33,366
Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) said: I would be very happy to spill yours.

946
01:06:33,882 --> 01:06:36,601
So, Amr(عمرو) was very upset and Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق) said;

947
01:06:36,960 --> 01:06:43,386
He draws out his sword as if it was a brand of fire, and they exchanged blows.

948
01:06:44,210 --> 01:06:47,917
And Amr(عمرو) strikes the shield of Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب),

949
01:06:48,585 --> 01:06:52,798
and the blow was so hard that the shield ended up hitting the head of Ali(علي)

950
01:06:52,929 --> 01:06:54,284
that was how powerful it was,

951
01:06:54,649 --> 01:06:58,095
 but on the other hand, because it was such a powerful blow

952
01:06:58,569 --> 01:07:00,339
the sword got stuck in the shield

953
01:07:00,735 --> 01:07:03,942
and Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) struck Amr(عمرو) in the neck,

954
01:07:04,923 --> 01:07:06,058
and he fell down dead,

955
01:07:06,579 --> 01:07:08,209
and the Sahabah(صحابه) made Takbeer(تكبير).

956
01:07:08,579 --> 01:07:11,239
And that's when Rasool Allah ﷺ knew that Ali Bin Abi Talib(علي بن ابي طالب) won.

957
01:07:12,110 --> 01:07:15,357
Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد ابن ابي وقاص) was a good marksman.

958
01:07:15,905 --> 01:07:21,833
So, he had in his sights, this enemy soldier, who was holding two shields.

959
01:07:22,532 --> 01:07:27,792
And it was sort of, you know, he was teasing the Muslims or what, but

960
01:07:28,362 --> 01:07:33,222
he would move down the shield a bit, so that the upper part of his head would show

961
01:07:33,262 --> 01:07:36,483
and then he would cover it again and then pull it down, up and down,

962
01:07:36,872 --> 01:07:41,598
so Sa'ad(سعد) aims at the man and fires his shot,

963
01:07:42,200 --> 01:07:43,997
while the shield was down,

964
01:07:44,402 --> 01:07:46,806
and it hits the man right in his forehead.

965
01:07:47,387 --> 01:07:50,005
So, the man falls down and his legs go up.

966
01:07:50,325 --> 01:07:54,556
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that and laughed, I mean, the way the man fell down was funny,

967
01:07:54,856 --> 01:07:55,986
so Rasool Allah ﷺ laughed.

968
01:07:56,731 --> 01:08:04,043
Sa'ad Ibn Muadh رضي الله عنه, Ayesha(عائشه) said: He was a tall and large man.

969
01:08:04,950 --> 01:08:09,837
And he was wearing armor but his arms were not covered.

970
01:08:10,294 --> 01:08:14,528
So Ayesha(عائشه) said: When I saw him, I was really worried about his arms,

971
01:08:15,184 --> 01:08:20,000
and Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), he was shot by an arrow in his arm.

972
01:08:20,762 --> 01:08:23,791
And it cut the main vein or artery in his arm.

973
01:08:24,466 --> 01:08:26,329
And he was seriously injured.

974
01:08:26,747 --> 01:08:33,027
So, these were some of the skirmishes that happened during the Battle of Al-Khandaq(الخندق).

975
01:08:33,412 --> 01:08:37,892
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

